{
  "paper": "I AM: The Root Speaks — Full Draft",
  "core_relation": {
    "sentence": "Knowledge of God depends on God's own self-disclosure (His speech), not only on creaturely upward inference; the two movements — reason climbing and God speaking — meet in the investigation.",
    "quote": "Reason climbs. God speaks. The investigation happens where those two meet. [S130][S131][S132]"
  },
  "product_test": {
    "answer": "multiplicative",
    "quote": "But if God has spoken, then the highest form of knowledge is not guessing correctly about a silent source. It is receiving the One who gives Himself to be known. [S117][S118]",
    "reason": "The paper frames disclosure as a necessary and non-substitutable condition: without God's speech, the whole investigation collapses back into 'guessing correctly about a silent source' (S117), and the conclusion ('the root is not silent... the root speaks' S140–S141) fails entirely. Upward inference is explicitly insufficient on its own (S096, S102), so the relation behaves multiplicatively — remove the disclosure factor and the paper's central claim goes to zero, not merely weaker."
  },
  "slots": [
    {
      "slot": "G",
      "plays_role": "God's self-disclosure / revelation as the external negentropy influx — coherence about the root cannot be generated from inside creaturely reasoning alone; it must come from outside, from God's own side.",
      "quote": "God is not first introduced as an object lying on a table, waiting for creatures to define Him. He is the One who calls, commands, creates, names, promises, judges, forgives, and reveals. [S012][S013]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "M",
      "plays_role": "Alignment between the disclosed name/character of God and the investigation — the name 'I AM' aligns the inquiry with God's own self-naming rather than with creaturely categories.",
      "quote": "It refuses to let God be measured from below. [S035]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "E",
      "plays_role": "Signal fidelity — whether the disclosure survives transmission through Scripture, interpretation, history, and the Church; the paper explicitly flags noise and distortion in the channel.",
      "quote": "Revelation can be misunderstood. Claims of revelation can be false. Scripture must be interpreted. History must be investigated. The Church can mishandle what it receives. [S112][S113][S114][S115][S116]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "S_eff",
      "plays_role": "Entropy as what lowers coherence — the paper treats creaturely reach, silent-source guessing, and mishandled revelation as the entropy that degrades knowledge of God.",
      "quote": "If God remains only an inference, then every argument about God stays trapped inside creaturely reach. [S096]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "T",
      "plays_role": "Temporal integration — God's speech and acts accumulate across covenant history and into Christ; the investigation happens over time as reason climbs and God speaks.",
      "quote": "God speaks. God acts. God covenants. God comes. God names Himself. God reveals His character. God enters the human story in Christ. [S104][S105][S106][S107][S108][S109][S110]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "K",
      "plays_role": "Compression — the divine name 'I AM' compresses God's self-existent, non-derived identity into a single boundary statement; ordered meaning compresses.",
      "quote": "That is not a slogan. It is a boundary. [S018][S019]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "R",
      "plays_role": "Phase transition — the shift from inference to disclosure is treated as a change of state, not degree: 'a different claim' that restructures the whole investigation.",
      "quote": "That is a different claim. [S125]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "Q",
      "plays_role": "Superposition — the disclosed portrait is stated before it is proven; the claim is held open for the skeptic until reality, reason, history, and experience converge.",
      "quote": "The disclosed portrait can be stated honestly before it is proven publicly. We can ask what Christianity claims. Then we can ask whether reality, reason, history, and experience converge with that claim. [S126][S127][S128]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "F",
      "plays_role": "Non-local correlation — the child/father analogy and the claim that the root enters history mean the knower and the known are not independent; related systems are coupled.",
      "quote": "And in Christ, Christianity says, the root walks into the room. [S142]",
      "fit": "stretched"
    },
    {
      "slot": "C",
      "plays_role": "Integration — the local integrator is the human knower who receives the One who gives Himself to be known; the meeting point of reason and revelation.",
      "quote": "It is receiving the One who gives Himself to be known. [S118]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    }
  ],
  "breaks": [
    "The paper treats upward inference (reason climbing) as genuinely valuable and not zero — 'Those arguments may matter. Some may be strong.' [S098][S099] — which softens the strict multiplicative collapse: reason is not a zero factor, so the product test is closer to 'disclosure is necessary but inference is additive support' than to a pure χ-style product.",
    "The 'child can hear his father speak' analogy [S053] imports a relational/personal factor that has no clean slot in the master equation's factor list; it is closer to a background condition than a multiplicative term.",
    "The paper explicitly disclaims that its claim proves itself: 'It does not prove by itself that Jesus is who Christianity says He is.' [S089] — so the slot mapping describes the shape of the claim, not a demonstrated derivation.",
    "Slot F is stretched: the paper's non-local correlation is theological (Christ as the root entering history) rather than a physical correlation between related systems."
  ],
  "extra_factors": [
    "Historical investigation / resurrection evidence [S091] — treated as a required support layer with no direct master-equation slot.",
    "The distinction between discovery and disclosure [S064][S065][S066] — a methodological factor the equation does not name.",
    "The skeptic's provisional stance [S120][S126] — a rhetorical/epistemic factor that conditions how the claim is received."
  ],
  "analog_strength": 3,
  "confidence": "medium",
  "one_line": "The paper's 'I AM' disclosure functions as the G-factor of the master equation: without God's self-speech the investigation collapses into guessing about a silent source, though the paper keeps upward inference as a non-zero additive support.",
